WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:06.660
This is chapter two of Learn
Text.js: Layout with Box.

2
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:10.010
The console is a grid of cells.

3
00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:13.930
You describe a layout with Box
and Tailwind-style class names.

4
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:18.140
Text.js turns them into Flexbox
properties and lays them out with Yoga,

5
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:22.970
the engine React Native uses, so Box
behaves the way you already expect.

6
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.650
Units are cells.

7
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:28.540
p-1 is one column and one row of padding.

8
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.740
Start with a top bar.

9
00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:39.970
Most screens are a column, with a one-row
bar on top and everything else below it.

10
00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:44.690
Import Spacer alongside
Box, Text and useInput.

11
00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:48.850
Then replace the title card with a
column that grows to fill the console.

12
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.610
The bar is a row.

13
00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:56.210
h-1 makes it exactly one cell tall, and
shrink-0 keeps it from being squeezed.

14
00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:01.170
Spacer is a box that grows, so anything
after it is pushed to the right edge.

15
00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:04.900
The row below takes the rest
of the height with grow.

16
00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:10.180
Next, a sidebar and cards.

17
00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:13.810
Add a Card component above the page.

18
00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:18.210
Each card is a bordered column with
one cell of padding on either side.

19
00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:22.850
grow, shrink and basis-0 give every
card an equal share of the row,

20
00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.210
whatever its content.

21
00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:28.130
minWidth and minHeight set
a floor, also in cells.

22
00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:31.620
NAV lists the sidebar's three items.

23
00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:36.130
In the page, keep two flags in state.

24
00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:39.770
One shows the sidebar, and
the other stacks the cards.

25
00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:44.010
Press s to toggle the sidebar,
and d to flip the direction.

26
00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:45.690
Then fill the row.

27
00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:50.570
The sidebar is 18 cells wide, with
a border on its right edge only.

28
00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:53.970
The cards sit in a row, or
in a column when stacked,

29
00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:56.250
with one cell of gap between them.

30
00:01:56.300 --> 00:02:00.940
In the row, items-start keeps them
from stretching to the full height.

31
00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:05.930
Here's the dashboard shell,
live on the lesson page.

32
00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:08.490
Click the pad so the page has focus.

33
00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:11.210
Press s, and the sidebar closes.

34
00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:13.210
Press it again to bring it back.

35
00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:16.570
Press d, and the cards
stack into a column.

36
00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:19.210
Press d again to put them back in a row.

37
00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.730
Each time, Yoga recomputes the layout

38
00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.610
and only the rows that
changed are encoded again,

39
00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:28.300
so every toggle is a single console.log.

40
00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:33.540
Finally, responsive layout.

41
00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:37.730
The grid follows the
docked DevTools panel.

42
00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:42.210
Drag the console narrower, and the cards
shrink to share the space that's left.

43
00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:44.690
Drag it wider, and they grow back.

44
00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:48.370
When you need breakpoints,
useBreakpoint returns the current one,

45
00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:56.500
measured in columns: sm from
60, md from 80, and lg from 110.

46
00:02:58.220 --> 00:02:59.290
Quick check.

47
00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:03.820
In className utilities,
what does p-1 mean?

48
00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:05.970
One cell.

49
00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:11.940
Units are terminal cells: one
column across, and one row down.

50
00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:17.060
Which class lets a box
take the remaining space?

51
00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:19.510
grow.

52
00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:26.520
It sets flexGrow to 1, exactly as in
CSS Flexbox, and Yoga does the layout.

53
00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:32.510
Next, in chapter three, you'll
style a deployment card with colors,

54
00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.750
text attributes and theme tokens.

55
00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:36.400
See you there.
